# C# Code Style

## DTOs as C# Records
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD
public record EventRequest(
    [Required(AllowEmptyStrings = false)] string Titulo,
    string? Descricao,
    [Required] DateTime? DataHora,
    string? Local,
    [Required][Range(1, int.MaxValue)] int? LimiteVagas);

public record EventResponse(long Id, string Titulo, string? Descricao, DateTime DataHora,
    string? Local, int LimiteVagas, int VagasRestantes);

// ❌ BAD — class with mutable properties and no value semantics
public class EventRequest { public string Titulo { get; set; } }
```

## Entities — explicit constructors, no Records
```csharp
public class Event
{
    public long Id { get; private set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public Event() { }               // required by EF Core

    public Event(string title, /* ... */) { Title = title; /* ... */ }

    public override bool Equals(object? obj) => obj is Event other && Id == other.Id;
    public override int GetHashCode() => Id.GetHashCode();
}
```
- Column/table names in Portuguese via `HasColumnName`/`ToTable` in `OnModelCreating` — never attributes on the entity
- `Equals`/`GetHashCode` based only on `Id`

## Dependency Injection — constructor only
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD
public class EventService
{
    private readonly IEventRepository _eventRepository;

    public EventService(IEventRepository eventRepository)
    {
        _eventRepository = eventRepository;
    }
}
```
Register everything in `Program.cs` (`AddScoped<IEventRepository, EventRepository>()`).
Never use service locators or static access to services.
